ShelfESP
========

ShelfESP is a client-side Fabric mod for Minecraft 26.1.2 that highlights
shelves containing at least one item, with the highlight rendered through
walls (an ESP-style overlay).

The rendering approach and the wide-line shader were inspired by the
open-source ChestESP mod by Alexander01998 (GPL-3.0-or-later):

    https://github.com/Wurst-Imperium/ChestESP

ShelfESP does not include ChestESP's code or assets. It implements its own
shelf scanner, configuration, key binding, renderer, and mixins. Its
depth-independent line/quad pipelines follow the same public Minecraft
rendering APIs that ChestESP uses, and the GLSL wide-line math is a
reimplementation of the standard screen-space line expansion used there.

